🧩 Functional Requirements
1. Lexicon Management
ID	Requirement
LEX-01	Define constants for entities (e.g., Ram, Socrates)
LEX-02	Define predicates for properties (e.g., Man(x), Mortal(x))
LEX-03	Define logical operators (e.g., ∀, ∃, →, ∧, ∨)
LEX-04	Handle different meanings of "is" (equality vs. class membership)
LEX-05	Support extensible lexicon (add new words easily)
2. Grammar & Parsing
ID	Requirement
GRM-01	Parse declarative statements (e.g., "Ram is a man")
GRM-02	Parse universal statements (e.g., "All men are mortal")
GRM-03	Parse existential statements (e.g., "Some men are wise")
GRM-04	Parse yes/no questions (e.g., "Is Ram mortal?")
GRM-05	Handle pronouns and anaphora resolution ("He is mortal")
GRM-06	Support at least 5-10 sentence patterns
GRM-07	Grammar must be extensible for future complexity
3. Semantic Translation
ID	Requirement
TRA-01	Translate "X is a Y" → IsA(X, Y) or Y(X)
TRA-02	Translate "All X are Y" → ∀x (X(x) → Y(x))
TRA-03	Translate "Some X are Y" → ∃x (X(x) ∧ Y(x))
TRA-04	Translate questions to logical queries (e.g., "Is X Y?" → ?- Y(X))
TRA-05	Preserve compositional meaning from grammar rules
4. Reasoning Engine
ID	Requirement
REA-01	Store facts in a knowledge base (FOL format)
REA-02	Perform forward/backward chaining to derive new facts
REA-03	Answer yes/no queries with logical proof
REA-04	Handle simple syllogisms (e.g., Socrates → mortal)
REA-05	Return "Unknown" when proof is not possible
REA-06	Explain the reasoning chain (optional but desirable)
5. Conversational Flow
ID	Requirement
CON-01	Accept structured English input (typed sentences)
CON-02	Distinguish between statements (learn facts) and questions (query facts)
CON-03	Accumulate knowledge across statements
CON-04	Respond with "Yes/No/Unknown" for questions
🔧 Non-Functional Requirements
ID	Requirement
NFR-01	Language: Python or Prolog (preference for Python)
NFR-02	Performance: Response time < 5 seconds for typical queries
NFR-03	Modularity: Separate modules for lexicon, grammar, translator, reasoner
NFR-04	Testability: Unit tests for each module
NFR-05	Extensibility: Add new grammar rules without breaking existing ones
NFR-06	Documentation: Clear documentation for all modules and APIs
NFR-07	Demonstration: Run with a preset knowledge base and test queries
🧪 Success Criteria
Must-Have (MVP)
